package com.makemission.ora.changelog

/** Kind of change, shown as a small label next to each line on the What's new page. */
enum class ChangeKind(val label: String) { ADDED("Added"), CHANGED("Changed"), FIXED("Fixed") }

/** One user-facing line about a change, written in plain words. */
data class ChangeItem(val kind: ChangeKind, val text: String)

/** The changes made on one date. Mirrors the entries in CHANGELOG.md; update both together. */
data class ChangeDay(val date: String, val items: List<ChangeItem>)

/** Newest first. Keep in step with CHANGELOG.md, per AGENTS.md rule 20. */
val Changelog: List<ChangeDay> = listOf(
    ChangeDay(
        date = "18 Nov 2026",
        items = listOf(
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "A page that fails to load is logged with the same plain words the error page uses (for example \"The address could not be found\") instead of a category and code number. Pages that fail because of a proxy or a bad address now get their own words too.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Installing an extension: tapping Add again while it is installing does nothing, the button says \"Adding…\", and the extension is installed once. A failed install now says why in plain words, not a blank message.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Pull to refresh reloads a page after a shorter pull, about 15% less than before, and a short haptic tick marks the moment the pull is far enough to reload.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "With the PIN lock on, asking for a private tab now shows the lock screen even when you are on a regular tab, so you can unlock from there. Before, the lock could stay on with no way to enter the PIN, and private tabs would not open.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Swiping the address bar moves only between tabs in the current space. From a normal tab it no longer lands on a private tab, and from a private tab it no longer lands on a normal one.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Links and images opened from a private tab (Open in new tab, Open in background tab, Open image in new tab) now open as private tabs instead of normal tabs. Nothing about them is logged.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Searches are no longer written to the log with the words you typed. The log now says only which search engine was used, for example \"Searched with Google\". Searches from a private tab leave no log line at all.  (commit pending)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "The app icon is no longer cropped on the home screen. The Ora mark now sits in the middle of Android's icon shape on its own charcoal background, and it also works with themed icons.  (`3232d02`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Fast downloads over http: Settings > Privacy > Network has a new switch, off by default. On, plain http:// files download in parts and can be paused and resumed, the same as https files. Off, plain http files download on one connection and cannot be paused. Their data is not encrypted, and the switch says so.  (`352ab8d`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Downloads are split into parts when the site allows it, and a dropped connection is retried. Unfinished downloads come back paused after Ora restarts, so you choose when to continue.  (`352ab8d`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "A \"Download started\" note appears at the bottom when a download begins and fades away by itself. Swipe it away if it covers something, or tap it to open Downloads.  (`352ab8d`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "On phone, the Downloads page opens as a sheet from the bottom that you can drag up to full screen. Pause is shown only on downloads that can pause.  (`352ab8d`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "A download that failed before it started is kept in the list after Ora restarts, so Retry is still there.  (`352ab8d`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Swipe down on the tablet's Compact row to see all your tabs. A swipe up on the phone's address bar already did this; now the tablet's top bar works the same way in reverse."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Tabs that were waiting to load when Ora was closed no longer lose their pages: they could be saved as blank, and open as a blank page."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "The Downloads page now matches the design: a summary of what is moving (count, speed and bytes left), an All, Active, Done and Failed filter, Active and Today sections, and rows with a file-type tile and a four-part progress bar. Finished files open on tap and share on a long press, and each filter has its own empty message. Pause, resume and retry are not in yet. Phone only so far."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "The Downloads page opens from the toolbar button and shrinks back into it when closed, and it has a Copy link action with a short confirmation on the details page. The tablet layout is not checked on a device yet."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Find in page now waits for you to finish typing, so a word that is on the page no longer shows \"No matches\", and the count starts at 1 instead of moving on with every letter you type."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Tabs waiting to load after Ora reopens now show their website name in the tablet sidebar and the tab list, instead of \"about:blank\"."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Search tabs, bookmarks and history in one field: on tablet, the sidebar's Tabs search now also lists matching bookmarks and history entries under your tabs, so you can find a page without choosing the right list first."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Drag a tab into a group: touch and hold a tab, then move your finger to pick it up, and drop it on a group card in the overview or on a group's header in the tablet sidebar. The group lights up as you hover over it. In the sidebar, drop a tab on \"Not in a group\" to take it out of its group. Holding a tab still without moving still opens Add to group, as before."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Inactive tabs: a tab you haven't opened for 14 days moves out of the way into a folded \"Inactive tabs (N)\" row, in the tab overview and in the tablet sidebar. Tap the row to open or fold it, and tap a tab inside to open it. Searching still finds them, tabs inside a group stay in their group, and private tabs are never moved."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Extensions screens: the list has a search that filters your installed extensions, a switch on each one, and a Get extensions row that opens addons.mozilla.org in a new tab. Tap an extension to see its version, what it can do (read from its permissions), Allow in private tabs (off unless you turn it on), Extension settings when it has a page for them, and Remove in red, which asks first. On tablet the list and the details sit side by side; on phone the details open as their own screen. Choosing who can use an extension on each site is not there yet."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Tab groups: long-press a tab (in the overview or the tablet sidebar) and choose Add to group to put it in a named, coloured group, or make a new one with a name and one of six colours. In the overview, groups are stacked cards; tap one to open its tabs, with Rename, Colour, Ungroup and Close group in its ⋯ menu. In the tablet sidebar, groups have headers that fold with a chevron, tabs outside any group sit under \"Not in a group\", and \"New tab group\" is at the bottom. Close group asks first. Groups are kept per profile and your tabs stay in their groups when Ora reopens. Private tabs can't be grouped."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "When Android rebuilds Ora's window, your open tabs now carry over instead of every tab being opened a second time.  (`bc21b78`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Reopened tabs no longer fail with \"Saved history is not valid\": tabs saved before their page had loaded were read back as broken history. They now reopen at their address, and a history that cannot be read is dropped instead of being saved again.  (`45fc871`)"),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "The log now keeps only the domain of a page (for example google.com), never the full address or what you searched for, and says nothing about what you do in private tabs. It is also kept between launches, up to about 5,000 lines, so an export covers days instead of one session, with the date on every line. Clear still empties it."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Private tabs now have their own list and numbering, separate from normal tabs, and the tab counts no longer include them. A private tab cannot be opened while Ora is locked (a notice says to unlock first), and a pop-up from a private tab opens as a private tab."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "Tabs reopened at start, or when you switch profile, now load only the tab you were on. The others load the first time you open them, so Ora starts faster and uses less data and memory. The notice says so."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Ora no longer starts twice when Android rebuilds its window right after launch: startup (crash handler, usage counts, app lock) runs once, and the window now survives font, density, language and similar changes. If a rebuild still happens, the log says so."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Quick resume no longer saves your tabs while they are still coming back, and an empty list never replaces a good save, so reopened tabs keep their own pages and history. Ora now says \"Reopened N tabs\" when it restores several."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Private space: a private tab turns the whole app Obsidian (Dark look only), its address bar gets a dashed Fog border and a \"Private\" chip, and the tab overview has a \"tabs | private\" switch. The private side lists tabs as rows with a dashed icon outline and no thumbnails, has a note on what is not saved, a dashed New private tab button, Lock private tabs (when App lock is set) and Close private, which closes every private tab in one tap. On tablet the sidebar has a pinned \"Private tabs (N)\" row that opens the same space inside the sidebar, with Back to tabs."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Profile tints: each profile can take a tint (Basalt, Moss, Clay, Tide or Plum) that colours Ora's own bars, sidebar and sheets in the Dark look. Web pages are never tinted, and Light and Pure dark ignore it. Long-press a profile chip to open its page: rename it, pick a tint and see it applied as you pick, with Cancel putting the old tint back. The + chip opens the same page for a new profile."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Find in page on tablet: it opens in the address bar's place, with the search icon, the text field, \"1 of 4\", previous, next and Done, and the field is ready to type at once. Back or Done brings the address bar back."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "The ⋯ menu panel on tablet no longer cuts off its top row: it starts below the top bar, has even space inside, and scrolls if it is taller than the screen."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "With the sidebar open on tablet, its button, Back and Forward move into the sidebar. The address bar, Tabs and ⋯ sit over the page, and the page sits in a rounded card."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "The speckled grain behind tiles and rows (the start page, Lab and Diagnostics) is gone. It was Android's press ripple; the press now only shrinks the tile a little."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "App lock: Settings > Privacy can ask for a PIN when Ora opens and whenever you come back to it. The PIN is kept only as a salted hash, never as the number itself. After five wrong tries you wait 30 seconds, then longer each time, and the lock screen counts it down."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "HTTPS-only mode: a Privacy switch that loads pages over a secure connection only."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Close all: the tab overview has a Close all button. It asks first, then opens one start page. The last 10 pages can be brought back from Reopen closed tab."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Add to home screen: a row in the ⋯ menu pins a shortcut to the current page, named after its title."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Text size on web pages: Settings > Appearance has − and + buttons that make page text smaller or larger, from 50% to 200%. Reset returns to 100% in one tap. It applies at once, with no reload."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "Copy page address: a row in the ⋯ menu copies the current page's address in one tap."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.ADDED, "With \"Count feature use\" on, swipes on the address bar, the edge swipe for the sidebar and pull to refresh are logged as worked or missed, with the reason and its distance and time. No page content is recorded. See Settings > Diagnostics."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "Mineral look: Light, Dark and Pure dark now use matte stone greys with chalk text. The selected state is a chalk fill with dark text."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "Ora now uses the Instrument Sans font throughout."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "On phones, the ⋯ menu has a new look: tiles for the main actions, plain rows below, and a Desktop site switch. A bookmarked page lights its Bookmark tile."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "The tab overview has the Mineral look on phone and tablet: the open tab has a Chalk ring, each tab shows an initial and a round close button, New tab is Chalk and Close all is red. The search box says how many tabs you have open, such as \"Search 9 open tabs\"."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "The Library has the Mineral look: round Bookmarks and History tabs, a round search box and a coloured letter beside each page. The History list on the tablet sidebar matches. Under your history it now says \"Private tabs are never saved.\""),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "The card a site shows when it asks for your camera, microphone, location or notifications has the Mineral look: an icon, a clear question, a red Block, a grey Not now and a light Allow. It now says that Not now asks again next time."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "Switching tabs now fades the page in instead of cutting over. With Remove animations on, it is instant."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "With a keyboard attached, Ctrl+Tab moves to the next open tab."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "On tablet, the sidebar now grows out of the sidebar button and shrinks back into it when it closes."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "On a tablet with a keyboard, Escape closes the sidebar."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.FIXED, "Auto-fill on a login page now reaches your password app. It no longer stops with \"Contents can't be auto-filled\"."),
            ChangeItem(ChangeKind.CHANGED, "When Auto-fill cannot help, the message says why: turn on a password app in your phone's settings, or tap a login field first, then reload the page if it still fails."),
        ),
